 <h1>What's New</h1>
 <p>The running log of what changed around here, newest first. We ship a lot. If something looks off after an update, hit the Report a problem button in the footer and we will get on it.</p>
 <h2>October 2026</h2>
+<li>Club Manager: your own transfers, and any club's fixtures. You asked to see every player you bought and sold, so the Latest tab in the <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a> transfer hub now has a Your club button that shows just your club's recorded deals: buys, sales and loans, newest first or biggest fee first. It lists what your save still keeps, so very old moves can be missing, and it says so. You also asked to click a club and see its fixtures: open any club and press Fixtures for every league game it plays this season, matchday by matchday, with the score where the save has it and Upcoming for the rest. Two smaller fixes as well. When the transfer desk turns you down, the note now sits at the bottom of the screen where you can see it and stays put while you scroll. And taking over a club in the middle of a season no longer hands you the last manager's unanswered decisions.</li>
+<li>Soccer Career: offers that wait for you, and a better phone. In <a href="/soccer-career">Soccer Career</a> a Life choice you had already been offered could disappear if your popularity dipped or you spent some money before you answered, even after a reload. Now an offer you already have stays on the table until you answer it. Your phone also gets an Ongoing stories list, so the esports team, the cursed boots, the teammate loan, the coaching course and the documentary show up there while they are still running. Two phone fixes too: the season limit on what chats can give you (karma, popularity and morale) now holds when you keep replying instead of quietly starting over, and a reply no longer reaches back and changes the save it started from.</li>
+<li>Club Manager: players other clubs buy stay bought. You told us a player who moved between two other clubs vanished from the game and turned up back at his old club the next season. In a <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a> career started after the 13 October update, that deal now sticks: he is in his new club's squad straight away, plays for them against you, shows up on the market at his new club (not for sale until the summer), and is still there next season. If your career is that new and already lost someone this season, opening it puts him back where he went. Careers started before that update keep the world they had.</li>
+<li>NBA, NFL, MLB and NHL My Career: retire from coaching, and take back a skip. Coaching after your playing days in <a href="/nba-my-career">NBA</a>, <a href="/nfl-my-career">NFL</a>, <a href="/mlb-my-career">MLB</a> and <a href="/nhl-my-career">NHL My Career</a> had no way out, so the seasons just kept coming. Now Retire from coaching ends it whenever you choose, after one check, and your record and coaching log stay saved. Hit Skip it at the draft showcase by mistake? Undo skip puts your draft stock back, any time before you press Draft day. And if you skipped through draft night, Watch it again plays it from the start.</li>
+<li>Club Manager: retire when you are ready, and see your highest scoring game. You asked how to retire in <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a>, and now you can: from the Manager panel between matches, from the season summary, or while you are out of work. It asks once, then your career ends with a farewell (your clubs, your trophy cabinet and your records) and stays in its slot as a finished career you can open any time. Your manager record also has a new line, the highest scoring game on your record. Careers saved before this update work it out from the scores they still keep, and say so if some are gone.</li>
+<li>Club Manager: No sacking. Want to stay at one club for life? Switch on No sacking when you start a career in <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a>, or later from Options. The board can still moan, it just can never fire you. It stays on for good, and that career stops posting leaderboard scores.</li>
+<li>Club Manager: the board judges the season you actually had. In <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a>, win the league, go up or give the board what it asked for and next season opens Safe, instead of a title season starting Under pressure. A new job, your first or any after it, starts high enough that one bad night usually leaves you Safe. The review now says when you went up, went down or stayed up when everyone had you going down (in the leagues where clubs move between divisions), and a sixth place finish no longer gets the statues. Offers come from clubs a step above yours (two steps after a top flight title or a Champions League win), so a small Danish club stops getting calls from the giants, and tapping one asks you first before anything moves. Taking over in mid season no longer hands you the last manager's failures, and a small club's good year pays a bonus its size can carry.</li>
+<li>Club Manager: your club is your squad on the market too. In a <a href="/club-manager">Club Manager</a> career you started before 13 October, or a Manager Hot Seat job you carried on, the transfer market still listed players at your own club who were not in your squad: the extra names on your club's real roster beyond the 26 you start with, and from your second season the men who had left you. Search your own club and you could buy from yourself. Not any more. The market lists nobody at your club, the same as your club's page, and the rest of the world in those careers plays on as it did.</li>
 <li>Player Bingo: Rodri counts on the Champions League square. <a href="/player-bingo">Player Bingo</a> could turn Rodri away on a Champions League winner square when his club seasons on our list had a gap. He won it with Manchester City in 2023, so now he counts there whatever his club history shows. It only covers that Rodri: anyone else with the same name still needs a winning club season to fill the square.</li>
 <li>World XI: every player's overall, and who shares a club. Once you play the season in <a href="/world-xi">World XI</a>, each player in your eleven shows his overall, the card rating the season was played with. The chemistry line now counts your club links, and a tap shows exactly which players share a club. They're just for fun, the season doesn't use them.</li>
 <li>Soccer Career: Luton Town in 2023, choices that say what they do, and rival offers that follow the usual veteran pay. If your <a href="/soccer-career">Soccer Career</a> lands in the 2023/24 Premier League, the one club that used to show up as another club is now Luton Town, who really were in that league. The results and the table are still your own season. Four Life choices now say exactly what they do: checking on your esports team, both ways out of the cursed boots, and turning up for the statue vote. And say yes to a rival club at 30 or older and their offer now goes through the same age and form check as any other move, so a veteran who has slipped takes a little less, one holding his level keeps the offer and an elite one can earn a raise.</li>
